For Automated Routing, can we configure 'Fallback Chains' based on real-time health checks? For example, if OpenAI has a 500 error, can the Gateway automatically re-route that specific payload to an equivalent Anthropic model without the client knowing?


"Can we implement 'Cost-Based Routing' where a request is routed to a smaller model (like GPT-4o-mini) if the prompt is simple, but upgraded to a flagship model only if the complexity or 'intent' warrants it?"

Why ask: This is a major "FinOps" win for a solution architect.

Questions on Prompt Management & Decorators
This is where you enforce "Guardrails" and "Company Standards" globally.

"In the Prompt Decorator plugin, can we enforce 'System Prompts' at the Gateway level that the developer cannot override? Specifically, for our Fraud domain, can we inject a hidden 'PII Redaction' instruction into every outbound request?"

Why ask: This ensures developers don't accidentally send sensitive bank data to an LLM.

"With Prompt Templates, how do we handle versioning? If we update a global 'Legal Compliance' template in Kong, is there a way to canary-test that new template version before it rolls out to all consuming applications?"

Why ask: It treats prompts like code (GitOps), which is vital for a Lead Architect.

"How does the Gateway handle 'Prompt Injection' protection when using these templates? Does it sanitize the user-provided variables before they are merged into the final LLM payload?"

Why ask: Security is the #1 concern for banks using AI.
